  "evidence": "TEXT_C: \"End privatisation; rapid GP access; universal NHS dentistry; +£8bn year one rising to £28bn; mental health therapies within 28 days\"; \"£15 minimum wage; raise Universal Credit by £40/week; scrap two‑child cap; Universal Basic Income ambition\"; \"Wealth tax (1% >£10m, 2% >£1bn); align CGT with earnings; 10:1 pay ratio cap; windfall taxes; public ownership of rail, water, and Big 5 energy\"; \"Cancel Trident; reform NATO with no‑first‑use; end routine stop‑and‑search; decriminalise sex work\"; strong sanctity/purity framing in environment and animal policies (e.g., \"Rights of Nature Act; ban blood sports; no new oil and gas; oppose new nuclear\"). TEXT_G: \"Legal right to see a GP within 7 days; recruit 8,000 more GPs; NHS dentistry guarantees; youth mental health hubs; free personal care; Carer’s Minimum Wage\"; \"Abolish business rates and replace with a Commercial Landowner Levy; tackle late payments; proper windfall tax; raise Digital Services Tax; close CGT loopholes; 4% levy on FTSE‑100 share buybacks\"; \"Merit‑based work visas; guarantee police attendance and investigation of all burglaries; cut court backlogs\"; equality and rights measures (PR/STV, votes at 16, renters’ rights, end Hostile Environment) without universalist redistributions like UBI; moderate authority stance (\"maintain nuclear deterrent; reverse Army cuts; target 2.5% of GDP on defence\").",
